 to find the maximum of\n","\\(f(x) = -0.8(x-3.5)^2 + 18\\) over the interval \\([-8, 9]\\).\n","\n","Start with the positions given below, take all initial velocities as zero, and run the algorithm for 8 iterations. Print the swarm after every iteration and compare the best value found with the analytical maximum."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","id":"psoq1101","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import numpy as np"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","id":"psoq1102","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["### 1. Objective function and starting swarm\n","\n","The fitness function has a single peak. Since the particles start at different points, the update step lets them move toward their own best positions and the best point seen by the swarm."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","id":"psoq1103","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def fitness(x):\n","    return -0.8 * (x - 3.5)**2 + 18\n","\n","positions = np.array([\n","    -7.2, -4.5, -1.8, 0.4, 2.1,\n","     4.8,  6.2,  7.7\n","], dtype=float)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","id":"psoq1104","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["### 2. PSO settings\n","\n","Here `w` controls how much of the previous velocity is retained, while `c1` and `c2` control the personal-best and global-best pulls."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","id":"psoq1105","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["n = len(positions)\n","velocities = np.zeros(n, dtype=float)\n","\n","w = 0.55\n","c1 = 1.4\n","c2 = 1.7\n","\n","lower_bound = -8\n","upper_bound = 9\n","max_iterations = 8"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","id":"psoq1106","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["### 3. Set the initial bests"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","id":"psoq1107","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["pbest_positions = positions.copy()\n","pbest_fitness = fitness(positions)\n","\n","best_index = np.argmax(pbest_fitness)\n","gbest_position = pbest_positions[best_index]\n","gbest_fitness = pbest_fitness[best_index]\n","\n","print(\"INITIAL SWARM\")\n","print(\"-\" * 57)\n","print(f\"{'Particle':>8} | {'Position':>10} | {'Fitness':>10}\")\n","for i in range(n):\n","    print(f\"{i + 1:8d} | {positions[i]:10.3f} | {fitness(positions[i]):10.3f}\")\n","\n","print(f\"\\nInitial global best: x = {gbest_position:.4f}, f(x) = {gbest_fitness:.4f}\")"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","id":"psoq1108","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["### 4. Run the iterations\n","\n","The random terms are generated at each iteration. Positions are clipped to the search interval, and personal/global bests are only updated when a higher fitness is found."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","id":"psoq1109","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["for iteration in range(max_iterations):\n","    r1 = np.random.rand(n)\n","    r2 = np.random.rand(n)\n","\n","    velocities = (\n","        w * velocities\n","        + c1 * r1 * (pbest_positions - positions)\n","        + c2 * r2 * (gbest_position - positions)\n","    )\n","\n","    positions = positions + velocities\n","    positions = np.clip(positions, lower_bound, upper_bound)\n","    current_fitness = fitness(positions)\n","\n","    improved = current_fitness > pbest_fitness\n","    pbest_positions[improved] = positions[improved]\n","    pbest_fitness[improved] = current_fitness[improved]\n","\n","    best_index = np.argmax(pbest_fitness)\n","    if pbest_fitness[best_index] > gbest_fitness:\n","        gbest_position = pbest_positions[best_index]\n","        gbest_fitness = pbest_fitness[best_index]\n","\n","    print(f\"\\nITERATION {iteration + 1}\")\n","    print(\"-\" * 69)\n","    print(f\"{'Particle':>8} | {'Position':>10} | {'Velocity':>10} | {'Fitness':>10}\")\n","    for i in range(n):\n","        print(\n","            f\"{i + 1:8d} | {positions[i]:10.4f} | \"\n","            f\"{velocities[i]:10.4f} | {current_fitness[i]:10.4f}\"\n","        )\n","    print(f\"Global best position: {gbest_position:.6f}\")\n","    print(f\"Global best fitness:  {gbest_fitness:.6f}\")"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","id":"psoq1110","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["### 5. Result and check\n","\n","For this quadratic, the peak is at \\(x=3.5\\), where the function value is 18. The stochastic PSO run may finish close to this point rather than landing on it exactly."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","id":"psoq1111","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["print(\"\\nFINAL RESULT\")\n","print(\"=\" * 39)\n","print(f\"Best position found : {gbest_position:.6f}\")\n","print(f\"Maximum fitness     : {gbest_fitness:.6f}\")\n","\n","exact_position = 3.5\n","exact_fitness = fitness(exact_position)\n","print(\"\\nANALYTICAL MAXIMUM\")\n","print(f\"Best position       : {exact_position:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Maximum fitness     : {exact_fitness:.2f}\")"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","id":"psoq1112","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["**Observation:** Compare the final PSO position with the analytical peak. Because the random coefficients differ between runs, the exact sequence of positions can change; the best fitness should approach 18."]}
